flowchart TB
%% From a firing rule to a person, and then on to the agent. Two exits, deliberately different.
%%
%% The paging exit wakes me. The agent exit only ever opens a pull request, so it arrives in the
%% same review queue with the same human at the end of it — just started without me being awake.
%%
%% Everything between the two exits is a filter, and the filters are the design. An alert name has
%% to be on a short written list before it is worth an agent run at all, and the poll is hourly
%% because the paging path has already reached me by then.

  rules["A rule fires<br/>(a file in git)"] --> am["Alertmanager<br/>groups, inhibits, routes, silences"]

  subgraph human["Reaches me"]
    direction TB
    ntfy["ntfy push<br/>severity: critical only"]
    alerts["#alerts<br/>the record, every severity"]
    secchan["#security<br/>policy and scan findings"]
  end

  am --> ntfy
  am --> alerts
  am --> secchan

  subgraph second["Reaches the agent"]
    direction TB
    detector["alert-detector<br/>hourly, and only for<br/>allow-listed alert names"]
    agent["Hermes<br/>investigates, then opens<br/>a pull request and stops"]
  end

  am --> detector
  detector -->|"one HMAC-signed POST,<br/>in-cluster only"| agent
  agent -->|"replies in channel"| alerts

  classDef gate fill:#121820,stroke:#71b7ff,stroke-width:2px,color:#e7edf3
  class detector gate
